  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-010', 'Discuss personal insights on the craft, processes, and challenges of composing fiction.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-011', 'WRITING THE WORLD – PUBLIC CREATIVE NONFICTION', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-012', 'The learner demonstrates understanding of the forms and conventions of public creative nonfiction, and how facts, research, and narrative techniques are woven together to inform, engage, and influence audiences. - Inquiry', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-013', 'Analyze public-facing creative nonfiction forms and genres (e.g., blogs, literary reportage, travelogue, advocacy narratives) in terms ideas, language, and structure.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-014', 'Evaluate how composers integrate elements of creative nonfiction (e.g., research, interviews, factual content) with voice to inform and engage audiences.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-015', 'Analyze how composers use and adapt elements of creative nonfiction to elucidate ideas and enhance impact.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-016', 'Examine ethical concerns in public-facing creative nonfiction, including accuracy, bias, privacy, and responsible representation. - Composition', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-017', 'Compose original public-facing creative nonfiction that integrates personal insight, factual material, and multimodal elements (e.g., photos, audio, video) to engage specific audiences.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-018', 'Apply strategies for ethical research in the creation of public-facing creative nonfiction.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-019', 'Revise one’s composition for clarity, tone, factual integrity, and coherence to make meaning and create impact appropriate for public audiences.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-020', 'Adapt different forms of delivery (bimodal or multimodal) and platforms (media) to present one’s public-facing creative nonfiction to various audiences. - Reflection', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-021', 'Reflect on how composing for public audiences influences narrative choices, ethical decisions, and style.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Composition 2', 12, 'G12-022', 'Evaluate how one’s composing can inform, persuade, or advocate, reflecting on responsibilities as a public- facing creative nonfiction composer.', NULL, NULL, 'Inquiry'),
  ('Creative Industries - Applied and Traditional Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'explain the definitions and domains of the creative industries in relation to Applied and Traditional Art and their impact on society and daily life;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Philippine Creative Industries in Applied and Traditional Arts A. Brief Background of Creative Industries B. Domains of the Creative Industry 1. Definition of Traditional and Applied Arts within the creative industries 2. Locating the Traditional and Applied Arts disciplines within the creative industries domains, such as: ● Traditional and Applied Arts ● Creative Services Domain ● Visual Arts Domains ● Audiovisual Media Domain ● Digital Interactive Media Domain (emerging cases) C. Local and Global Cases and Situations 1. Practices, applications, and ethical considerations. 2. Intercultural sensitivity D. Artisans, designers, and cultural practitioners as creative enablers E. Career pathways 1. Craft entrepreneurship 2. Product design 3. Cultural heritage preservation 4. Creative production and design services F. Creative markets, platforms, and cultural entrepreneurship'),
  ('Creative Industries - Applied and Traditional Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'analyze the relevance and implications of prevailing creative industry laws and regulations on the production of applied and traditional art production;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Laws Related to Creative Industries and Applied/Traditional Arts A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (Republic Act no. 11904) B. Indigenous Peoples Rights Act (IPRA) C. UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples (UNDRIP) D. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) 1. Nature 2. Key functions/ Purpose E. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) 1. Nature 2. Key functions and purposes F. Intellectual Property Rights (Republic Act no. 8293) 1. Core Intellectual Property Concepts ● Trademarks, patents, copyrights, trade secrets and design protection ● Moral, economic, and other related rights ● Licensing and product branding G. Real-World Intellectual Property Concerns 1. Cultural appropriation 2. Fair use and Creative Commons 3. Infringement and misuse of indigenous designs 4. Generative AI and design ownership H. Department of Economy, Planning and Development (DepDev) and RA no. 11904 Implementation in Relation to Applied and Traditional Arts 1. DepDev’s specific responsibilities under RA 11904 2. Alignment with the Philippine Development Plan (PDP)'),
  ('Creative Industries - Applied and Traditional Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'conduct industry mapping for the applied and traditional arts sector to illustrate the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key players within the industry;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping in Applied and Traditional Arts A. Introduction to Industry Mapping 1. Definition and purpose of industry mapping 2. Applications in design and craft industries B. Key players in the industry (e.g., artisans, designers, craft producers, suppliers, distributors, retailers, cultural communities, regulators) C. Mapping the Value Chain in craft and Design Production D. Roles, Responsibilities, and Corresponding Rights of Artisans and Designers'),
  ('Creative Industries - Applied and Traditional Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'apply techniques in the production of an applied or traditional art output with consideration of ethical, safety, and industry practices;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements and Principles of Applied and Traditional Arts A. Forms of Applied and Traditional Arts 1. Crafts (woodcraft, basketry, handicrafts) 2. Ceramics and pottery 3. Textile arts and weaving 4. Product and industrial design 5. Epics and Oral Forms (e.g. chants) B. Materials and Techniques in Applied and Traditional Arts C. Production Process 1. Concept development 2. Selection of materials 3. Craftsmanship and finishing 4. Presentation and distribution D. Scope and Complexity of the Output 1. Craft prototypes 2. Design concepts 3. Documentation of local craft traditions 4. Small collaborative exhibitions'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-001', 'explain the historical development of dance within the Philippine creative industries and its impact on Philippine society and everyday cultural practices;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Dance in the Philippine Creative Industries A. Historical Development of Dance in the Philippines 1. Pre-colonial period 2. Colonial period'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-002', 'analyze the relevance and implications of creative industry laws and legal frameworks for dance production and choreographic ownership;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Policies and Laws Governing Creative Industries A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (Republic Act No. 11904) 1. Creative Industry Domains Relevant to Dance: • Performing Arts Domain • Audiovisual Media Domain • Digital Interactive Media Domain • Creative Services Domain • Traditional Cultural Expressions Domain B. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) C. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHIL) D. Intellectual Property Rights (RA8293) as applied to choreography and performance 1. Copyrights and moral rights'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-003', 'develop an industry map illustrating the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key stakeholders in the dance sector;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping A. Process of industry mapping 1. Identify the industry sector 2. Identifying key stakeholders 3. Categorizing roles and functions 4. Analyzing relationships and collaborations 5. Presenting the industry structure through charts or diagrams B. Key players in the dance industry (e.g., choreographer, dancer, artistic director, producer, technical director, stage manager, critic, presenter, festival organizer)'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how the elements of artistic expression interact and contribute to the overall impact of a dance performance;', NULL, NULL, 'Elements of Artistic Expression in Dance A. Elements of Dance: Body, Energy, Space, Time B. Choreographic principles and composition C. Organic unity in Dance 1. Content 2. Form 3. Audience Reception'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-005', 'examine potential safety hazards and risks associated with dance practices and processes and evaluate the effectiveness of safety protocols; and', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Safety Protocols and Procedures in Dance A. Physical factors in the work environment (e.g., flooring, lighting, ventilation) B. Body conditioning and injury prevention C. Risk assessment and management in rehearsals and performances D. Workspace safety and hazard control E. Proper care and use of equipment and facilities F. Dancer health, body maintenance, and ergonomics NOTE: This topic/content can be included in the apprenticeship courses.'),
  ('Creative Industries - Dance', 12, 'G12-006', 'create dance studies that integrate elements, skills, and techniques while demonstrating originality and artistic expression.', NULL, NULL, 'V. Artistic Expression in Dance A. Dance Fundamentals and Styles 1. Philippine Dance Traditions ● Indigenous dances ● Regional folk dances 2. Hispanic and American Influences on Philippine Dance 3. Transformations in Philippine Dance'),
  ('Creative Industries - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the definitions and domains of the creative industries in relation to Literary Arts and their impact on society and daily life;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Philippine Creative Industries in Literary Arts A. Brief Background of Creative Industries 1. Domains of Creative Industries 2. Definition and manifestations of literary arts within the creative industries 3. Societal impact of literary arts as a creative industry specific to publishing and print media B. Local and global cases and situations in literary publishing and print media 1. Practices, applications, and ethical considerations 2. Intercultural sensitivity and diversity in literary arts practice'),
  ('Creative Industries - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'infer the relevance and implications of prevailing creative industry laws for literary production and publication;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Policies and Laws Related to Creative Industries A. Legal concerns relevant to creative industries 1. Copyright in literary works 2. Moral and economic rights of authors 3. Publishing contracts and licensing B. Sectors related to creative industry laws 1. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) 2. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHIL) C. Laws related to creative industries 1. Philippine Creative Industries Act (Republic Act no. 11904) 2. Intellectual Property Rights (Republic Act no. 8293)'),
  ('Creative Industries - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'conduct industry mapping for the literary arts sector to represent the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key players within the industry; and', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping in Literary Arts A. Introduction to industry mapping 1. Definition and purpose 2. Applications in publishing and writing careers B. Key players and creative enablers in the literary industry (e.g., author, editor, publisher, literary agent, distributor, bookseller, critic, reader) C. Mapping the value chain in literary production and distribution D. Roles, responsibilities, and corresponding rights of writers and literary practitioners'),
  ('Creative Industries - Literary Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'apply literary techniques in producing a creative written work with consideration for ethical, safety, and industry practices.', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements and Principles of Literary Expression A. Forms of literary art 1. Fiction 2. Non-fiction 3. Poetry 4. Essays and short stories'),
  ('Creative Industries - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the definitions and domains of the creative industries, with a focus on Media Arts, and their impact on society and daily life;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Philippine Creative Industries A. Brief Background of Creative Industries B. Domains of the Creative Industry 1. Definition of Media Arts within the creative industries 2. Locating the different media arts disciplines within the creative industries domains, such as: ● Audiovisual media - film, television, animation, etc. ● Digital interactive media - web design, video games, AR/VR content, etc. ● Creative services - advertising, media consultancy, photo-video coverage services, etc. ● Design - graphic design, production design, logo and visual design, etc. ● Publishing and Print - text articles, illustration, print layout, graphic design, etc. ● Performing arts - dance films, video art, experimental performance media, etc. ● Visual arts - photography, animation, mixed-media and video art, etc. C. Challenges and opportunities facing the Philippine media arts industries 1. Globalization and market competition 2. Funding and audience sustainability 3. Digital platforms and global audiences 4. Innovation and technology'),
  ('Creative Industries - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'infer the relevance and implications of prevailing creative industry laws for media production;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Laws Related to Creative Industries and Media Arts A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (Republic Act No. 11904) B. Intellectual Property Rights (Republic Act No. 8293) 1. Core Intellectual Property Concepts ● Trademarks, Patents, and Copyright in audiovisual and digital works ● Moral, Economic, and other Related Rights ● Licensing and distribution rights C. Real-World Intellectual Property Concerns in Media Arts 1. Copyright infringement and digital piracy 2. Fair Use and Creative Commons 3. Plagiarism, Infringement, and IP Theft 4. Generative AI and Intellectual Property Ownership Note: Discussion cases on creative works in relation to intellectual property concepts and issues (see sample/suggested cases for class discussion below).'),
  ('Creative Industries - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'conduct industry mapping for the media arts sector to represent the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key players within the industry; and', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping in Media Arts A. Introduction to Industry Mapping 1. Definition and purpose of industry mapping 2. Applications in media production and creative careers (e.g. job hunting, business planning, policy development) B. Key players in the media arts industry (e.g., director, producer, editor, cinematographer,'),
  ('Creative Industries - Media Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'apply media arts techniques in producing a creative work with consideration of ethical, safety, and industry practices.', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements and Principles of Media Arts Artistic Expression A. Forms of media arts 1. Photography 2. Film and video 3. Animation 4. Graphic and digital design 5. Interactive and multimedia production B. Elements of media composition (e.g., framing, color, sound, editing, sequencing, narrative structure, visual hierarchy, typography, visual communication) C. Media production process 1. Concept and project development 2. Preproduction and planning 3. Production and postproduction 4. Publishing and distribution D. Exploration of platforms and venues for media exhibition (print, broadcast, digital, social media) E. Ethical use and proper attribution of digital content and generative artificial intelligence (AI) tools'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-001', 'discuss the historical development of music within the Philippine creative industries and its impact on Philippine society and everyday cultural practices;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Music in the Philippine Creative Industries A. Historical Development of Music in the Philippines 1. Pre-colonial period 2. Colonial period 3. Post-colonial and contemporary periods 4. Music within the Philippine Creative Industries B. Local and Global Cases and Situations 1. Practices, applications, and ethical considerations'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-002', 'explain the relevance and implications of prevailing creative industry laws and other legal matters for music production;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Policies Governing Creative Industries A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (RA no. 11904) 1. Creative Industry Domains Relevant to Music: ● Performing Arts Domain ● Audiovisual Media Domain ● Digital Interactive Media Domain ● Creative Services Domain ● Traditional Cultural Expressions Domain B. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) C. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) D. Intellectual Property Rights (RA no. 8293) as applied to music 1. Copyright and neighboring rights 2. Moral and economic rights 3. Licensing and performance rights E. Real-World Intellectual Property Concerns 1. Copyright infringement 2. Fair use and Creative Commons 3. Plagiarism and sampling issues 4. Generative artificial intelligence (AI) and music ownership F. Department of Economy, Planning and Development (DepDev) and RA no. 11904 Implementation in relation to Music 1. DepDev’s specific responsibilities under RA no. 11904 2. Alignment with the Philippine Development Plan (PDP)'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-003', 'conduct industry mapping for the music sector to represent the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key players within the industry;', NULL, NULL, 'B. Key players in the music industry (e.g., composers, arrangers, performers, producers, sound engineers, managers, promoters, distributors, critics) C. Roles, responsibilities, and corresponding rights of music artists and creatives'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how the elements of music interact and contribute to the overall impact of a music performance or composition;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements of Artistic Expression in Music A. Elements of Music: Melody, Harmony, Rhythm, Texture, Timbre, Form, Dynamics B. Organic unity in music performance 1. Content 2. Form 3. Audience reception'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-005', 'examine potential safety hazards and risks associated with music practices and processes to evaluate the effectiveness of safety protocols; and', NULL, NULL, 'V. Safety Protocols and Procedures in Music A. Physical factors in the work environment (e.g., acoustics, stage setup, electrical equipment) B. Safety training for musical instruments and equipment C. Risk assessment and management in rehearsals and performances D. Workspace safety and hazard control E. Proper care and maintenance of instruments and equipment F. Musicians’ body mechanics and hearing protection NOTE: This topic/content may be incorporated into the Apprenticeship Courses.'),
  ('Creative Industries - Music', 12, 'G12-006', 'create a music performance or composition that integrates elements, skills, and techniques, demonstrating originality and artistic expression.', NULL, NULL, 'VI. Artistic Expression in Music A. Elements of music in performance and composition B. Voice and/or instrument training C. Ensemble coordination D. Rehearsal and staging E. Performance criteria and evaluation'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'explain the historical development of theater within the Philippine creative industries and its impact on Philippine society and everyday cultural practices;', NULL, NULL, '2. Colonial period 3. Post-colonial and contemporary periods 4. Theater within the Philippine Creative Industries B. Local and Global Cases and Situations 1. Practices, applications, and ethical considerations. 2. Intercultural sensitivity 3. Theater and its impact on society and everyday cultural practices C. Theater artists and production teams as creative enablers'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'analyze the relevance and implications of creative industry laws and legal frameworks for theater production and the authorship of dramatic works;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Policies Governing Creative Industries and Theater A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (RA no. 11904) 1. Creative Industry Domains Relevant to Theater: • Performing Arts Domain • Audiovisual Media Domain • Creative Services Domain • Traditional Cultural Expressions Domain B. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) C. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) D. Intellectual Property Rights (RA no. 8293) as applied to Theater Arts 1. Copyright in scripts and performances 2. Moral rights, economic rights, and other related rights 3. Licensing and performance rights E. Real-World Intellectual Property Concerns in theater 1. Plagiarism and infringement 2. Fair use and Creative Commons'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'develop an industry map illustrating the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key stakeholders in the theater arts sector;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping in Theater A. Process of industry mapping 1. Identify the industry sector 2. List key stakeholders 3. Categorize roles and functions 4. Analyze relationships and collaborations 5. Present the industry structure visually through charts or diagrams B. Representation of key players in theater (e.g., playwrights, directors, actors, stage managers, set designers, costume designers, lighting designers, producers, critics, audiences) C. Roles, responsibilities, and corresponding rights of theater practitioners'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'analyze how the elements of artistic expression interact and contribute to the overall impact of a theater performance;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements of Artistic Expression in Theater A. Elements of Theater: script, character, plot, setting, dialogue, spectacle, and performance B. Elements of stage production: set, costume, lighting, sound, and props C. Organic Unity in Theater'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-005', 'examine potential safety hazards and risks associated with theater practices and production processes and evaluate the effectiveness of safety protocols; and', NULL, NULL, 'V. Safety Protocols and Procedures in Theater Arts A. Physical factors in the work environment (stage layout, lighting equipment, electrical setup) B. Safety training (use of tools and equipment) C. Risk assessment and management D. Workspace safety and hazard control E. Proper care and use of materials and equipment F. Actor’s body and voice care NOTE: This topic/content may be integrated into the Apprenticeship Courses.'),
  ('Creative Industries - Theater Arts', 12, 'G12-006', 'create a mini-theater production that integrates elements, skills, and techniques demonstrating originality and artistic expression.', NULL, NULL, 'VI. Integration of Artistic Expression in Theater Arts A. Fundamental concepts in drama B. Body, voice, and movement C. Acting styles and techniques D. Rehearsal and staging processes E. Performance criteria and evaluation'),
  ('Creative Industries - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-001', 'explain the historical development of Visual Arts within the Philippine creative industries and its impact on Philippine society and everyday cultural practices;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Overview of Visual Arts in the Philippine Creative Industries A. Historical Development of Visual Art in the Philippines: Pre-colonial to Contemporary Development B. The Philippine Creative Industries 1. Definition of Visual Arts as a key sector industry 2. Other visual arts-related industries C. Local and Global Cases and Situations 1. Practices, applications, and ethical considerations 2. Intercultural sensitivity 3. Visual Art and its impact on society and everyday cultural practices D. The Visual Artist as Creative Workforce Enablers'),
  ('Creative Industries - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-002', 'infer the relevance and implications of prevailing creative industry laws on art production;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Policies and Laws Related to Creative Industries A. Philippine Creative Industries Act (Republic Act no. 11904) 1. Nature 2. Key Features 3. Domains Relevant to Visual Arts B. World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) 1. Nature 2. Key functions and Purpose C. Intellectual Property Office of the Philippines (IPOPHL) 1. Nature 2. Key functions and Purpose D. Intellectual Property Rights (Republic Act 8293) 1. Core Intellectual Property Concepts ● Trademarks, Patents, Copyrights, Trade Secrets ● Moral, Economic, and other Related Rights'),
  ('Creative Industries - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-003', 'conduct industry mapping for visual arts to accurately represent the roles, relationships, and interdependencies of key players within the industry;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Industry Mapping in Visual Arts A. Industry Mapping 1. Introduction to Industry Mapping ● Definition and purpose of industry mapping ● Real-life applications (e.g. job hunting, business planning, policy development) B. Key players in the visual arts industry (e.g., artists, illustrators, graphic designers, art directors, printmakers, production specialists, curators, gallery owners or managers, art dealers or agents, platform providers, collectors, critics) C. Mapping the value chain in visual arts production and distribution'),
  ('Creative Industries - Visual Arts', 12, 'G12-004', 'apply visual arts techniques in producing a creative output, with appropriate safety practice;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Elements and Principles of Visual Arts Artistic Expression A. Forms of Visual Arts 1. Drawing 2. Painting 3. Sculpture 4. Printmaking 5. Mixed Media and Installation Art 6. Digital and Contemporary Visual Art B. Visual Art Composition 1. Elements of Art- line, shape, form, color, value, texture, space 2. Principles of Design - balance, contrast, emphasis, movement, pattern, rhythm, unity, proportion C. Visual Art Production Process 1. Concept development and ideation 2. Sketching and planning 3. Creation and experimentation with materials and techniques 4. Presentation, exhibition, and documentation of artworks D. Exploration of Art Spaces and Platforms for Art Exhibition - galleries, museums, public spaces, art fairs, online galleries, and digital platforms'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-001', 'propose discipline-specific creative productions grounded in artistic research and cultural contexts;', NULL, NULL, 'I. Creative Research and Concept Development A. Artistic Inquiry and Ideation (Discipline-Specific) 1. Exploration of themes, concepts, and artistic questions 2. Study of references and influences B. Cultural and Audience Context 1. Analysis of cultural, social, or community context 2. Identification of target audience and purpose C. Concept and Proposal Development 1. Formulation of creative concept and artistic direction 2. Articulation of intent, message, and relevance 3. Preliminary description of format 4. Justification of concept based on research'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-002', 'plan collaborative andcreative productions using industry- based processes within their chosen art forms;', NULL, NULL, 'II. Collaborative Planning and Design A. Discipline-specific preparations and collaborative explorations (ex. choreography, script writing, composition, storyboarding, curatorial plan) B. Roles and collaborative workflows'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-003', 'execute discipline-specific creative productions using appropriate artistic, technical, and technological processes;', NULL, NULL, 'III. Creative Execution and Iteration A. Artistic development and prototyping B. Use of tools, media, and technologies C. Rehearsal, drafting, editing, and fabrication D. Feedback integration and refinement'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-004', 'present discipline-specific creative works for public engagement following professional standards;', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Public Presentation and Audience Engagement A. Modes of presentation (e.g., performance, exhibition, screening, publication, and digital platforms) B. Technical and aesthetic execution C. Audience engagement strategies D. Application of professional standards and protocols in presentation'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-005', 'document the creative production process and outputs using industry-standard formats within the chosen discipline; and', NULL, NULL, 'V. Documentation and Portfolio Development (Integrated Across Phases) A. Process documentation (e.g., journals, recordings, and drafts) B. Compilation of outputs (e.g., portfolio, production book, and manuscript) C. Production reports and digital archiving'),
  ('Creative Production and Presentation', 12, 'G12-006', 'evaluate discipline-specific creative productions through critique and reflective analyses.', NULL, NULL, 'VI. Critical Evaluation and Reflection A. Feedback and critique systems B. Evaluation of artistic and technical quality C. Reflective analysis of process and output'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-001', 'Naipaliliwanag ang kahulugan, kahalagahan, at katangian ng wika sa komunikasyon at ang papel nito sa lipunan', NULL, NULL, 'I. Batayang Kaalaman sa Wika A. Kahulugan at Kahalagahan ng Wika sa Komunikasyon B. Katangian ng Wika 1. Arbitraryo 2. Dinamiko 3. Malikhain 4. Iba pa I. Batayang Kaalaman sa Wika'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-002', 'Nasusuri ang gamit at tungkulin ng wika sa sarili, pamilya, lipunan, bansa, at daigdig', NULL, NULL, 'C. Gamit at Tungkulin ng Wika 1. Interaksiyonal 2. Instrumental 3. Regulatoryo 4. Heyuristiko 5. Impormatibo 6. Personal 7. Imahinatibo'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-003', 'Naibabahagi ang mga halimbawang sitwasyon na nagpapakita ng mga gamit at tungkulin ng wika', NULL, NULL, 'C. Gamit at Tungkulin ng Wika 1. Interaksiyonal 2. Instrumental 3. Regulatoryo 4. Heyuristiko 5. Impormatibo 6. Personal 7. Imahinatibo'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-004', 'Naihahambing ang paggamit ng mga barayti ng wika ayon sa mga piling sitwasyong napakinggan, nabasa, at napanood', NULL, NULL, 'D. Barayti ng Wika 1. Idyolek 2. Dayalek 3. Sosyolek 4. Rehistro E. Wikang Pambansa, Wikang Panturo, Wikang Opisyal, Bilingguwalismo, at Multilingguwalismo'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-005', 'Nasusuri ang barayti ng wika na ginamit sa teksto batay sa layon, konteksto, at target na awdyens', NULL, NULL, 'D. Barayti ng Wika 1. Idyolek 2. Dayalek 3. Sosyolek 4. Rehistro E. Wikang Pambansa, Wikang Panturo, Wikang Opisyal, Bilingguwalismo, at Multilingguwalismo'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-006', 'Naiuugnay ang mga konseptong pangwika sa iba’t ibang sitwasyong pangkomunikasyon batay sa sariling kaalaman, pananaw, at mga karanasan', NULL, NULL, 'D. Barayti ng Wika 1. Idyolek 2. Dayalek 3. Sosyolek 4. Rehistro E. Wikang Pambansa, Wikang Panturo, Wikang Opisyal, Bilingguwalismo, at Multilingguwalismo'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-007', 'Naiisa-isa ang mga sanhi at bunga ng mahahalagang pangyayari sa pag-unlad ng wikang Filipino', NULL, NULL, 'II. Pag-unlad ng Wikang Filipino A. Mga Katutubong Wika B. Tagalog C. Pilipino D. Filipino III. Mga Sistema ng Pagsulat sa Pilipinas A. Mga Katutubong Sistema ng Pagsulat B. Alpabeto 1. Abecedario 2. Abakada 3. Alpabetong Filipino (Walong dagdag na letra at mga tuntunin sa pagbabaybay)'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-008', 'Naipaliliwanag ang sistema ng pagsulat at ang mga batayang tuntunin sa pagbabaybay sa Filipino', NULL, NULL, 'II. Pag-unlad ng Wikang Filipino A. Mga Katutubong Wika B. Tagalog C. Pilipino D. Filipino III. Mga Sistema ng Pagsulat sa Pilipinas A. Mga Katutubong Sistema ng Pagsulat B. Alpabeto 1. Abecedario 2. Abakada 3. Alpabetong Filipino (Walong dagdag na letra at mga tuntunin sa pagbabaybay)'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-009', 'Nasusuri ang mga sitwasyong pangwika sa Pilipinas mula sa mga napakinggan, nabasa, at napanood', NULL, NULL, 'IV. Mga Sitwasyong Pangwika sa Pilipinas A. Edukasyon B. Midya C. Pamahalaan D. Kalakalan E. Batas F. Iba pa'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-010', 'Nakasusulat ng kritikal na sanaysay na tumatalakay sa sitwasyon ng wikang Filipino sa lipunang Pilipino', NULL, NULL, 'Awtput: Kritikal na Sanaysay'),
  ('Filipino 1 (Wika at Komunikasyon sa Akademikong Filipino)', 12, 'G12-011', 'Naipaliliwanag ang kahulugan, kahalagahan, uri, antas, elemento, at proseso ng komunikasyon', NULL, NULL, 'I. Konseptong Pangkomunikasyon A. Kahulugan at Kahalagahan ng Komunikasyon B. Uri ng Komunikasyon 1. Berbal 2. Di-berbal C. Antas ng Komunikasyon 1. Intrapersonal 2. Interpersonal 3. Publiko'),
